# unit-watch-timing.vrs: unit-watch D28 (tick budget with every watch rule running). The dev events.json holds uw-timing-a,
# uw-timing-b, uw-timing-c and uw-timing-d (tools/vrclient/fixtures/uw-timing-*.json: waveList SpawnWaves of 12 then 6
# CHAR_Spider_Forest, wave 2 after 60 s, 30 min; a at the pond (-1880, -1640), b 125 m north (-1880, -1515), c 125 m east
# (-1755, -1640), d 125 m south (-1880, -1765)) and apo-test (tools/vrclient/fixtures/apo-test.json); together 72 spiders
# plus the apocalypse's roamers and horde, 50 or more tracked. Chaos stands at uw-a (the pond); at the measured span's
# start uw-timing-d's units are marked by `.nyar event unstick` (A3: a sunk unit does not stay sunk), so recovery, its
# landing checks and the removals run while the watch reads every unit, its off-ground reads included.
# The roamers find Chaos at the pond and hunt him, so every window has hunt targets. About 12 min after the first health
# line with 50 or more tracked, every event is stopped; the orchestrator runs `pwsh tools/preflight.ps1 -TimingSpan <log
# copy> -Windows 10 -MinTracked 50` on the log copy and reads the "watch" phase in the slowest-phase lines.
#
# Needs: a Release DLL with unit-watch step 3; the five entries above enabled, every other spawning definition disabled;
# [Debug] TimingLog = true (VerboseLogging optional); [UnitWatch] Enabled = true, StuckSeconds 90, StallMinutes 30 (for this run only: a 10-minute backstop clears the quiet
# last waves inside the span), and apo-test's hordes.firstAfterMinutes 15 in the dev events.json for this run only (at 1 the
# first horde reaches the goal about 8 min in and the apocalypse ends "lost" before the measured span);
# [Limits] MaxUnitsPerWave 12 or more and MaxTrackedUnits 150 (the default); NyarDevTools (.devtp, .devgo)
# and DevChatEcho; vrclient with `calc` and `expect-calc`; Chaos invulnerable (`ToggleInvulnerable true`, a Boolean, never
# false).
# Run: --var AX=-1880 --var AZ=-1640 --var BX=-1880 --var BZ=-1515 --var CX=-1755 --var CZ=-1640
ensure
console ToggleInvulnerable true
wait 2
console TPHome
wait 3
chat .nyar event reload
expect-log events: reloaded
chat .nyar status
expect-reply tracked units: 0 ( timeout=40
chat .devtp ${AX} ${AZ}
expect-log \[DEV TP\] to x=(?P<PX>-?[0-9.]+) y=-?[0-9.]+ z=(?P<PZ>-?[0-9.]+)
wait 4
console ToggleInvulnerable true
wait 2
chat .devmarks
expect-reply uw-rock
mark
chat .nyar event start uw-timing-a
expect-log event uw-timing-a wave 1/2 timeout=30
chat .nyar event start uw-timing-b
expect-log event uw-timing-b wave 1/2 timeout=30
chat .nyar event start uw-timing-c
expect-log event uw-timing-c wave 1/2 timeout=30
chat .nyar event start uw-timing-d
expect-log event uw-timing-d wave 1/2 timeout=30
chat .nyar event start apo-test
expect-log event apo-test started by manual timeout=20
wait 10
chat .devgo uw-a
expect-log \[DEV TP\] uw-a
wait 4
console ToggleInvulnerable true
wait 2
chat .nyar status
expect-log \] tracked units: (?P<T1>[0-9]+) \( timeout=10
expect-calc ${T1} >= 50
shot full uw-timing-start
# the measured span starts at the first health line with 50 or more tracked (every 10 min from boot)
expect-seen nyar health: [45] events, ([5-9][0-9]|[1-9][0-9][0-9]) tracked timeout=660
# A3: uw-timing-d's units marked by `.nyar event unstick` at the measured span's start (a sunk unit does not stay sunk), so
# recovery and its landing checks run inside it; their removal about 5 min later leaves a, b and c's 54 tracked
chat .nyar event unstick uw-timing-d
expect-reply units marked
expect-seen \[nyar\] unit-watch uw-timing-d stuck: CHAR_Spider_Forest wave [12] \(admin\) timeout=30
expect-seen \[nyar\] unit-watch uw-timing-d recovered: CHAR_Spider_Forest try 1/2 timeout=30
wait 300
chat .nyar status
expect-log \] tracked units: (?P<T2>[0-9]+) \( timeout=10
expect-calc ${T2} >= 50
wait 360
chat .nyar status
expect-log \] tracked units: (?P<T3>[0-9]+) \( timeout=10
expect-calc ${T3} >= 50
shot full uw-timing-end
chat .nyar event stop uw-timing-a
expect-log event uw-timing-a stopped
chat .nyar event stop uw-timing-b
expect-log event uw-timing-b stopped
chat .nyar event stop uw-timing-c
expect-log event uw-timing-c stopped
# uw-timing-d ended on its own: the removal of its marked units cleared both waves
expect-seen event uw-timing-d ended: all waves defeated \(2 of 2 waves\) timeout=5
chat .nyar event stop apo-test
expect-log event apo-test stopped
wait 30
chat .nyar status
expect-reply tracked units: 0 timeout=40
console TPHome
wait 3
